{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-haiku-5-5","id":"msg_011ChK5XKDJZhzNHJUCHqLKh","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"`saveAll` now waits for every write before it resolves. The fix is in `store.js`:\n\n```js\nasync function saveAll(items, db) {\n  await Promise.all(items.map((item) => db.put(item.id, item)));\n  return items.length;\n}\n```\n\nThe cause was `items.forEach(async ...)`. `forEach` ignores the promises its async callback returns, so `saveAll` returned `items.length` straight away. Callers could continue before the `put` calls had finished. A failed write also became an unhandled rejection instead of rejecting `saveAll`. `Promise.all` fixes both: the function resolves only after all writes succeed, and it rejects if any write fails.\n\nThe existing test in `test/store.test.js` passes. I ran it by file path (`node --test test/store.test.js`). My first run passed the `test/` directory, which made Node try to load it as a test file and report a failure. That was a problem with the command, not the code.\n\nI didn't add a test for the failure path or for a slow `put`. A test where `put` is delayed and checks that all items are saved before `saveAll` resolves would catch this regression directly. I can add it if you want."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":400,"cache_read_input_tokens":24634,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":400},"output_tokens":8,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global","speed":"standard"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"0e96c515-12a9-4c6a-b4a1-131dec4e55fd","uuid":"594472f9-d9d7-44d9-8807-a3289ccf8a05","timestamp":"2026-11-23T02:34:22.958Z","request_id":"req_011ChK5XK3tLGiad7CCXXrhQ"}
